@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: ships are a taught unit class — move, fire, and siege contact — not a flavour slide
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no ship unit type exists under the sandbox
'   checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning engine and tutorial
'   modules before a covers: line can be honest.
'   siege contact this must not fake .... _spec/_plans/tutorial-siege-lines.puml
'   the runner that may sequence it ..... _spec/_plans/tutorial-interactive-siege.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "ships" is a UNIT CLASS beat. The player has to move (or fire, or land) a
' ship under live rules. Flavour art with a caption is not the item.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   water-only, air, or a named hull
'   whether ships place, cut, or ignore siege lines
'   combat vs transport as the first verb
'
' If ships never touch siege lines, this beat can ship before the siege
' runner. If they do, the line type has to exist or the contact is painted.
title PLANNED — a ship the player actually drives;\nnot a caption over hull art

component "ship unit (engine)" as SHIP <<app>>
component "first verb\nmove · fire · land" as VERB <<app>>
component "tutorial beat" as BEAT <<app>>
component "**flavour slide**\nno ship is issued" as SLIDE <<error>>
component "siege line contact" as LINE <<app>>
component "interactive siege runner" as RUN <<app>>

BEAT ARROW_MAIN VERB
VERB ARROW_MAIN SHIP
BEAT ARROW_ERROR SLIDE
SHIP ARROW_OPTIONAL LINE
RUN ARROW_OPTIONAL BEAT

note bottom of SLIDE
  **Hull illustration is not a unit class, because
  a beat that never issues a ship order did not
  land.** Unlock one verb and require the player
  to apply it against the live unit.
end note

note bottom of LINE
  **Contact with siege lines remains optional
  until the live unit demonstrates it.** If ships
  ignore lines, do not teach a bounce; if they cut
  or halt, this beat waits on the line type.
end note

note right of VERB
  **One verb is sufficient for the first ship
  lesson: movement or fire, not an entire
  campaign.** Additional verbs conceal which rule
  the player missed when the beat fails.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Find the unit.** Movement domain, attack, and whether a siege line is
  terrain to a ship. That last fact decides whether this beat is inside the
  siege runner or a free-standing lesson.
  --
  **2. Teach one verb against the live unit.** Fail if the order never hits
  a ship. Do not autoplay a crossing.
  ==
  **3. Sequence after lines only if contact is real.** Otherwise ship this
  beat on its own so siege work is not blocked on hull art.
  --
  **Left open**: hull types; fog; whether tanks and mecha share this lesson
  or stay on land.
end legend
@enduml
